Package: DFBM
Title: Denoising abundance matrices by factorizing binary masks
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: 
    person("Mukai", "Wang", , "wangmk@umich.edu", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-1413-1904"))
Description: A nonparametric denoising method for nonnegative abundance matrices
    (samples by features). Each column is dichotomized into a nested sequence of
    binary masks at its own quantile thresholds. The masks are factorized jointly
    into low-rank probability matrices by proximal gradient descent with singular
    value thresholding, giving each entry an estimated survival curve over the
    thresholds. The denoised value is the capped expectation implied by that
    curve, which fills in zeros and caps extreme values. New samples are
    denoised with the fitted factors, without refitting.
